# St. Joseph River Watershed & Environmental Monitoring Network

## Project Overview

This GIS project visualizes the spatial configuration of an environmental
monitoring network within the St. Joseph River watershed in northern Indiana
and southwestern Michigan.

The map integrates watershed boundaries, elevation data, river and tributary
networks, flowlines, and environmental monitoring locations to provide
spatial context for watershed-scale water-quality research.

## Map Features

- Watershed and sub-basin boundaries
- Digital Elevation Model (DEM)
- River and tributary network
- Detailed hydrologic flowlines
- Environmental sampling locations
- ND-LEEF monitoring location
- Sampling-basin location within the broader watershed

## Monitoring Locations

The mapped monitoring network includes:

- Niles
- APH
- NDGC
- HC
- NDBH
- BAKER
- MISH
- WC
- ND-LEEF

